ontent": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment."}], "type": "post_instructions"}], "id": 12}], "stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "id": 0, "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome"}, {"_data": [], "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n1le01ob12re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe8n1le01ob12re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<span class= \"strong\">Sam</span>: Look at this, Helen. I'm reading this book about business, and I have a good idea to implement this information into our current business process diagram for the company. <br>\n<span class= \"strong\">Helen</span>: What are those tables? <br>\n<span class= \"strong\">Sam</span>: These are the diagrams. We can use one of them to show our business processes in an organized and punctual way. Many companies are currently using them to represent their business processes graphically; I am now creating my own diagram."}, {"time": "29000", "image": "enpe8n1le01ob12re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class= \"strong\">Helen</span>: What are the components of the diagram? <br>\n<span class= \"strong\">Sam</span>: Well, there are the actors. An actor is an entity who makes decisions or takes action inside the business process; as you can see, each actor is standing on a swim lane. We use arrows to connect their actions. <br>\nIf we get to a point where we need to make a decision, we use a diamond to indicate the existence of a decision point. <br>\n<span class= \"strong\">Helen</span>: Okay, I understand the symbols and arrangement now. What business processes do we represent with the diagram? <br>\n<span class= \"strong\">Sam</span>: Do you remember the As-Is and To-Be processes? <br>\n<span class= \"strong\">Helen</span>: Sure. <br>"}, {"time": "68000", "image": "enpe8n1le01ob12re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class= \"strong\">Sam</span>: Okay. With this diagram, we can show both of these processes. We start by analyzing the current state of the business. Then, we take information from the clients; their point of view is quite important, and it can facilitate reaching the goals. From that information, we can determine the current barriers and the possible solutions to overcome them; this is exactly the point we are at with our current business process analysis. The next steps are designing the process based on the data we have, develop and implement it. I am currently organizing everything to start this part of the process. <br>\n<span class= \"strong\">Helen</span>: Thanks for your time and explanation.<br>\n<span class= \"strong\">Sam</span>:: You are welcome."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n1le01ob12re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "template_override": 1, "id": 1, "title": ""}, {"_data": [], "contents": [{"value": {"video_src": "enpe8n1le01ob12re5vsc01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "", "id": 0, "text": ""}]}, "type": "video"}], "type": "video", "template_override": 1, "id": 4, "title": ""}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "type": "scholar"}]}